{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","prediction_set_name":"k2-horizon-high-full200-2026-09-29","paper_id":"2411.03264","judge_input_sha256":"9b44a71a6db6f4f0d1c8dbb46b8ab03ea144ffebba3655d68d2f310fc1dc5e72","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2411.03264:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2411.03264:I002:U001","2411.03264:I002:U002","2411.03264:I002:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U003"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is failure to derive the accumulated sum of derivative jumps because earlier jumps are absent from the energy estimate. ISSUE-002 instead identifies an incorrect Young-inequality parameter and absorption calculation; it does not diagnose the missing earlier-jump terms.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2411.03264:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2411.03264:I003:U001","2411.03264:I003:U002","2411.03264:I003:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold concern is that an admitted first-slab degree p=1 makes integrated-projector and reconstruction definitions undefined or false. ISSUE-001 diagnoses a wrong endpoint derivative index for the projector, without recognizing the p=1 domain omission or the independent reconstruction failure.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2411.03264:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2411.03264:I004:U001","2411.03264:I004:U002","2411.03264:I004:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is misuse of L2 inner products and orthogonality under a generic Banach-space hypothesis, repaired by restricting X to a Hilbert space. ISSUE-001 instead concerns incompatible endpoint conditions in the integrated projector and does not identify the missing Hilbert-space structure.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2411.03264:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2411.03264:I005:U001","2411.03264:I005:U002","2411.03264:I005:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U002","ISSUE-002:U003"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is an unattainable spatial approximation exponent in the elliptic projection estimate. ISSUE-002 identifies a reciprocal epsilon error in a stability proof, not an invalid spatial-order bound.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2411.03264:I006","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2411.03264:I006:U001","2411.03264:I006:U002","2411.03264:I006:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U004","ISSUE-003:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold defect is that inner-product quantities and a squared-norm argument in the reconstruction require a Hilbert space, while the stated hypothesis is only Banach. ISSUE-003 instead concerns insufficient temporal and spatial regularity for L2-valued Laplacian jumps in the reliability proof.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}